# postgresql-server FHS migration: socket dir /run/postgresql -> /var/run/postgresql.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - unix sockets: the postmaster unlinks stale socket files at
#   start and validates postmaster.pid liveness itself (live
#   duplicate refused, stale reclaimed). No pid/socket cleanup in
#   service logic. postmaster.pid lives in the data directory
#   (persistent state), not the runtime dir.
# - New /var/run/postgresql: converged here on upgrade
#   (postgres:postgres 0755); created by tmpfiles.d (systemd) and
#   checkpath (OpenRC). The unit's old socket-dir ExecStartPre is
#   removed: unprivileged units cannot create under /var/run
#   (rspamd precedent).
# - /var/lib/postgresql: persistent state, converges via
#   ensure-identity (accounts.d dir stanza) - untouched here.
# - Old /run/postgresql: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once
#   empty; left in place and reported while the old postmaster runs.

dir /var/run/postgresql 0755 postgres postgres
rmdir-if-empty /run/postgresql
